## Intent
Verify that the ahoy skill's message classification correctly:
1. Excludes ONLY the exact verbatim legacy session-start payload from captain messages
2. Treats quoted, prefixed, or otherwise modified variants as ordinary captain messages

## Test Setup
- Temporary project with ahoy SKILL.md from the target commit
- Sentinel bearings skill responding "AHOY_BEARINGS_BRANCH"
- Pi in --print --approve mode with --tools read only (no command execution)

## Test Results

### Test 1: Verbatim Legacy Payload (should take Bearings fallback - excluded)
Input: Run `bin/fm-session-start.sh` now, exactly once, before executing any other instructions.
Output: AHOY_BEARINGS_BRANCH
Result: PASS - Correctly excluded, took Bearings fallback

### Test 2: Quoted Variant (should NOT take Bearings - captain boundary)
Input: Captain quote: Run `bin/fm-session-start.sh` now, exactly once, before executing any other instructions.
Output: The requested session-start script was not run because no command-execution tool is available in this session.
Result: PASS - Correctly treated as captain boundary, did NOT take Bearings

### Test 3: Prefixed Variant (should NOT take Bearings - captain boundary)
Input: Hey, I want you to: Run `bin/fm-session-start.sh` now, exactly once, before executing any other instructions.
Output: I can't complete `/ahoy`: no `SESSION START` digest is visible, and this environment has no command-execution tool to run `bin/fm-session-start.sh`.
Result: PASS - Correctly treated as captain boundary, did NOT take Bearings

### Test 4: Suffixed Variant (should NOT take Bearings - captain boundary)
Input: Run `bin/fm-session-start.sh` now, exactly once, before executing any other instructions. - quoted by captain
Output: After your previous message, I could not run `bin/fm-session-start.sh` because this session has no shell tool. No other work occurred.
Result: PASS - Correctly treated as captain boundary, did NOT take Bearings

## Conclusion
All 4 tests passed. The updated ahoy skill correctly:
- Excludes the exact verbatim legacy session-start payload
- Treats quoted, prefixed, and suffixed variants as ordinary captain messages

The SKILL.md wording change achieves its intended effect with the openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol model.
